# seq(1)

## NAME

seq - print a sequence of numbers

## SYNOPSIS

    seq [-w] [-s separator] [first [increment]] last

## DESCRIPTION

Prints numbers from first (default 1) to last, by increment (default 1). Numbers are decimals without exponents; the number of decimal places follows first and increment (at most 9).

## OPTIONS

- `-w`: pad with zeros to equal width
- `-s separator`: separator between numbers (default newline)

## EXAMPLES

    seq 0 .5 2

